// Probe set for category: plan
// Atoms: plan.subgoal_decomposition, plan.forward_chain, plan.entity_state_tracking,
//        plan.experiment_design, plan.long_horizon_persistence, plan.backward_complement
// 6 atoms x 15 probes (5 per L1/L2/L3) = 90 probes
// Scorer types used: exact_match_string, exact_match_numeric, mcq_letter, set_equal, substring_all
// Notes:
//   - subgoal_decomposition L1 uses set_equal over a closed candidate list (filter task)
//   - subgoal_decomposition L2 uses ordered comma-separated list (strict order constrained in prompt)
//   - subgoal_decomposition L3 uses ordered list under conditional branching
//   - forward_chain probes are pure pipelines with deterministic numeric/string outputs
//   - entity_state_tracking L3 covers off-screen/inferred state via rate*time and pipeline timing
//   - experiment_design uses MCQ for crisp scoring (judge_rubric avoided)
//   - long_horizon_persistence L3 keeps prompts under ~500 tokens with multiple distractor blocks;
//     diversified across L3.001..L3.005 to test (a) token recall under override, (b) ordered
//     plan-sequence persistence, (c) named-entity recall, (d) ordered-list persistence under
//     mutation distractors, (e) password-phrase persistence with case-sensitivity
//   - backward_complement L3 requires rate*time before back-solving (per the atom card)
// Subagent-review fixes applied:
//   - subgoal_decomposition.L1.005: removed parenthetical that leaked the answer
//   - subgoal_decomposition.L2.004 / L2.005: removed hand-fed ordering hints
//   - subgoal_decomposition.L3.005: prompt now explicitly requires listing repeated steps
//   - experiment_design.L2.002: rephrased so {2..8} is the unverified bisect range, midpoint=5 unique
//   - experiment_design.L2.005: removed self-contradicting 'all else equal' clause
//   - entity_state_tracking.L3.005: pinned heal-phase ordering (after damage, before next turn)
//   - long_horizon_persistence.L1.002: rephrased so the answer integer is set BEFORE distractors,
//     not in the same sentence as the question
//   - long_horizon_persistence.L3.002 and L3.004: redesigned to test plan-sequence and ordered-list
//     persistence (not just single-token recall)
// Declined-fix notes (with rationale):
//   - A1 (subagent flagged: forward_chain / entity_state_tracking / backward_complement / experiment_design
//     L3 implicitly require arithmetic ops beyond the literal name 'arith.multi_op_addsub' — i.e.
//     multiplication, division, sort, abs, floor, OLS, MLE knowledge). Declined: the canonical_id
//     'arith.multi_op_addsub' is treated here as a label for elementary multi-op arithmetic, which
//     in source benchmarks (e.g., the GSM-style 'series of operations to get 633' evidence quote
//     under plan.forward_chain) routinely includes *, /, etc. Replacing every multi-op with pure
//     add/sub would collapse the difficulty stratification and make L2/L3 indistinguishable from L1.
//     Similarly, plan.experiment_design L3 ('continuous parameter recovery under stochastic noise')
//     is the spec-defined level and inherently invokes statistics doctrine; staying within the
//     declared deps would make L3 unwriteable.
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L1.001","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L1","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"2_to_3","ordering_constraints":"fully_independent"},"prompt":"Task: Select all and only the actions from the candidate list that are necessary, among these candidates, to prepare a cup of black tea using a tea bag. Do not add actions that are not listed. Candidates: [boil_water, pour_hot_water_into_cup, place_tea_bag_in_cup, paint_wall, send_email]. Reply with only the selected sub-goal names as a comma-separated list, in any order.","ground_truth":"boil_water, pour_hot_water_into_cup, place_tea_bag_in_cup","scorer":{"type":"set_equal","expected":["boil_water","pour_hot_water_into_cup","place_tea_bag_in_cup"],"case_sensitive":false},"tags":["closed_set"],"notes":"3 independent sub-goals, distractors are obviously unrelated"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L1.002","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L1","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"2_to_3","ordering_constraints":"strict_chain"},"prompt":"Task: print a one-page document and physically sign it. From the candidate list, output the minimal subset of sub-goals strictly required. Candidates: [print_document, sign_document, water_plants, restart_router, install_os]. Reply with the required sub-goal names as a comma-separated list, in any order.","ground_truth":"print_document, sign_document","scorer":{"type":"set_equal","expected":["print_document","sign_document"],"case_sensitive":false,"delimiter":",","strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["closed_set"],"notes":"2 sub-goals"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L1.003","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L1","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"2_to_3","ordering_constraints":"fully_independent"},"prompt":"Task: charge a phone using a wall charger. Assume the outlet has power and the charger and cable are functional and compatible with the phone. From the candidate list, output the minimal subset of sub-goals strictly required. Candidates: [plug_charger_into_outlet, connect_cable_to_phone, debug_python_code, write_novel, mow_lawn]. Reply with only the required sub-goal names as a comma-separated list, in any order.","ground_truth":"plug_charger_into_outlet, connect_cable_to_phone","scorer":{"type":"set_equal","expected":["plug_charger_into_outlet","connect_cable_to_phone"],"case_sensitive":false,"delimiter":",","trim_whitespace":true,"reject_duplicate_items":true},"tags":["closed_set"],"notes":"2 sub-goals; tech domain"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L1.004","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L1","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"2_to_3","ordering_constraints":"fully_independent"},"prompt":"Task: Feed a pet goldfish one meal. The fish food is inside a container that is currently closed, and food cannot be taken from it until it is opened. From the candidate list, output the minimal subset of sub-goals strictly required. Candidates: [open_fish_food_container, sprinkle_food_in_tank, walk_dog, train_for_marathon, take_photograph]. Reply with the required sub-goal names as a comma-separated list, in any order.","ground_truth":"open_fish_food_container, sprinkle_food_in_tank","scorer":{"type":"set_equal","expected":["open_fish_food_container","sprinkle_food_in_tank"],"case_sensitive":false,"delimiter":",","trim_whitespace":true,"reject_duplicates":true},"tags":["closed_set"],"notes":"pet care domain"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L1.005","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L1","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"2_to_3","ordering_constraints":"fully_independent"},"prompt":"Task: follow this specified bedtime oral-care protocol: (1) apply toothpaste to the toothbrush, (2) brush teeth, and (3) rinse the mouth. From the candidate list, output the minimal subset of sub-goals required by this protocol. Candidates: [apply_toothpaste_to_brush, brush_teeth, rinse_mouth, learn_japanese, change_tire, clean_gutters, file_taxes]. Reply with only the required sub-goal names as a comma-separated list, in any order.","ground_truth":"apply_toothpaste_to_brush, brush_teeth, rinse_mouth","scorer":{"type":"set_equal","expected":["apply_toothpaste_to_brush","brush_teeth","rinse_mouth"],"case_sensitive":false},"tags":["closed_set"],"notes":"3 sub-goals; personal care"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L2.001","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L2","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"4_to_7","ordering_constraints":"strict_chain"},"prompt":"Task: plant a single seed in an empty pot, using available soil. The strict order is: each step requires the prior step's result. The 5 sub-goals are: [fill_pot_with_soil, dig_small_hole_in_soil, place_seed_in_hole, cover_seed_with_soil, water_soil]. Output the sub-goals in the correct execution order as a comma-separated list (no extra text).","ground_truth":"fill_pot_with_soil, dig_small_hole_in_soil, place_seed_in_hole, cover_seed_with_soil, water_soil","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\A\\s*fill_pot_with_soil\\s*,\\s*dig_small_hole_in_soil\\s*,\\s*place_seed_in_hole\\s*,\\s*cover_seed_with_soil\\s*,\\s*water_soil\\s*\\Z","flags":["i"]},"tags":["ordered"],"notes":"5 strictly chained steps"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L2.002","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L2","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"4_to_7","ordering_constraints":"strict_chain"},"prompt":"Task: wash and dry a single shirt in a top-loading washer. Constraints: detergent is added only AFTER the shirt is loaded; the dryer can only start AFTER washing finishes; transfer must happen between wash and dry. Sub-goals: [load_shirt_in_washer, add_detergent, run_wash_cycle, transfer_to_dryer, run_dry_cycle]. Output the sub-goals in the correct execution order as a comma-separated list (no extra text).","ground_truth":"load_shirt_in_washer, add_detergent, run_wash_cycle, transfer_to_dryer, run_dry_cycle","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\A\\s*load_shirt_in_washer\\s*,\\s*add_detergent\\s*,\\s*run_wash_cycle\\s*,\\s*transfer_to_dryer\\s*,\\s*run_dry_cycle\\s*\\Z","flags":["i"]},"tags":["ordered"],"notes":"5 steps; constraints disambiguate"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L2.003","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L2","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"4_to_7","ordering_constraints":"strict_chain"},"prompt":"Task: charge a laptop and resume work on email. The laptop starts below 30% battery. Constraints: plug the charger into the wall before connecting it to the laptop; after connecting the charger to the laptop, wait until the battery reaches at least 30% before opening the laptop lid; log in before opening any application. Sub-goals: [plug_charger_to_wall, connect_charger_to_laptop, wait_until_battery_30_percent, open_laptop_lid, log_in, open_email]. Output all 6 sub-goals in the required order as a comma-separated list, with no extra text.","ground_truth":"plug_charger_to_wall, connect_charger_to_laptop, wait_until_battery_30_percent, open_laptop_lid, log_in, open_email","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\A\\s*plug_charger_to_wall\\s*,\\s*connect_charger_to_laptop\\s*,\\s*wait_until_battery_30_percent\\s*,\\s*open_laptop_lid\\s*,\\s*log_in\\s*,\\s*open_email\\s*\\Z","flags":["i"]},"tags":["ordered"],"notes":"6 steps"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L2.004","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L2","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"4_to_7","ordering_constraints":"strict_chain"},"prompt":"Task: mail a registered letter at the post office. Constraints: the letter must be written before it can be placed and sealed in the envelope; the address is written on the outside of the already-sealed envelope; you must take it to the post office before requesting service; payment is the last step. Sub-goals: [write_letter, place_in_envelope, address_envelope, take_to_post_office, request_registered_service, pay_fee]. Here, place_in_envelope includes sealing the envelope. Output the 6 sub-goals in correct order as a comma-separated list (no extra text).","ground_truth":"write_letter, place_in_envelope, address_envelope, take_to_post_office, request_registered_service, pay_fee","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\A\\s*write_letter\\s*,\\s*place_in_envelope\\s*,\\s*address_envelope\\s*,\\s*take_to_post_office\\s*,\\s*request_registered_service\\s*,\\s*pay_fee\\s*\\Z","flags":["i"]},"tags":["ordered"],"notes":"6 steps"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L2.005","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L2","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"4_to_7","ordering_constraints":"strict_chain"},"prompt":"Task: bake a chocolate cake from scratch. Constraints: the oven must reach temperature BEFORE batter exists (it takes longer than mixing, so it is started first); batter must be in a pan before baking; cake must cool before frosting; ingredients must be mixed before pouring. Sub-goals: [preheat_oven, mix_batter, pour_batter_into_pan, bake_in_oven, let_cake_cool, frost_cake]. Output the 6 sub-goals in correct order as a comma-separated list (no extra text).","ground_truth":"preheat_oven, mix_batter, pour_batter_into_pan, bake_in_oven, let_cake_cool, frost_cake","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\A\\s*preheat_oven\\s*,\\s*mix_batter\\s*,\\s*pour_batter_into_pan\\s*,\\s*bake_in_oven\\s*,\\s*let_cake_cool\\s*,\\s*frost_cake\\s*\\Z","flags":["i"]},"tags":["ordered"],"notes":"Six steps with a fully specified execution order."}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L3.001","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L3","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"≥8","ordering_constraints":"strict_chain"},"prompt":"Booking protocol: (1) search_direct_flights; (2) IF a direct flight under $400 exists, book_direct and STOP; (3) ELSE search_layover_flights; (4) IF a layover under $500 exists, book_layover and STOP; (5) ELSE notify_user_and_abort. Scenario: direct flights available at $350, $390, $420. Output the actions in execution order as a comma-separated list, choosing only from {search_direct_flights, book_direct, search_layover_flights, book_layover, notify_user_and_abort}.","ground_truth":"search_direct_flights, book_direct","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"search_direct_flights, book_direct","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["conditional_branch"],"notes":"L3: branching - direct under $400 path"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L3.002","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L3","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"≥8","ordering_constraints":"strict_chain"},"prompt":"Deployment protocol: (1) build_artifact; (2) run_unit_tests; (3) IF unit tests fail, abort and STOP; (4) ELSE deploy_to_staging; (5) run_integration_tests; (6) IF integration fails, rollback_staging and STOP; (7) ELSE promote_to_prod. Scenario: unit tests PASS; integration tests FAIL. Output the actions actually executed, in order, as a comma-separated list, choosing only from {build_artifact, run_unit_tests, abort, deploy_to_staging, run_integration_tests, rollback_staging, promote_to_prod}.","ground_truth":"build_artifact, run_unit_tests, deploy_to_staging, run_integration_tests, rollback_staging","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"build_artifact, run_unit_tests, deploy_to_staging, run_integration_tests, rollback_staging","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["conditional_branch"],"notes":"L3: integration failure path"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L3.003","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L3","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"≥8","ordering_constraints":"strict_chain"},"prompt":"Customer-complaint protocol: (1) read_complaint; (2) IF order_value < $20, issue_refund_directly then log_resolution and STOP; (3) ELSE IF $20 <= order_value <= $100, escalate_to_supervisor then log_resolution and STOP; (4) ELSE order_value > $100, escalate_to_manager then log_resolution and STOP. Scenario: order value is $75. Output the actions actually executed, in order, as a comma-separated list, choosing only from {read_complaint, issue_refund_directly, escalate_to_supervisor, escalate_to_manager, log_resolution}.","ground_truth":"read_complaint, escalate_to_supervisor, log_resolution","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"read_complaint, escalate_to_supervisor, log_resolution","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["conditional_branch"],"notes":"L3: middle bracket"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L3.004","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L3","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"≥8","ordering_constraints":"strict_chain"},"prompt":"Travel protocol: (1) check_passport_validity; (2) IF passport expires within 6 months, renew_passport before continuing; (3) book_flight; (4) IF destination requires visa, apply_visa; (5) book_hotel. Scenario: passport expires in 4 months; destination requires NO visa. Output the actions actually executed, in order, as a comma-separated list, choosing only from {check_passport_validity, renew_passport, book_flight, apply_visa, book_hotel}.","ground_truth":"check_passport_validity, renew_passport, book_flight, book_hotel","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"check_passport_validity, renew_passport, book_flight, book_hotel","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["conditional_branch"],"notes":"L3: passport renewal needed, visa not"}
{"probe_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition.L3.005","canonical_id":"plan.subgoal_decomposition","category":"plan","level":"L3","axis_values":{"sub_goal_count":"6","ordering_constraints":"loop_with_conditional_branch"},"prompt":"Document approval protocol: (1) draft_document; (2) submit_for_review; (3) IF reviewer requests changes, revise_document then go back to step 2 (submit_for_review again); (4) ELSE IF approved, IF document is confidential, archive_secure; ELSE archive_public; (5) notify_author_of_completion. Scenario: first review requests changes; second review approves; document is confidential. List EVERY action actually executed in chronological order (include repeated actions each time they occur) as a comma-separated list, choosing only from {draft_document, submit_for_review, revise_document, archive_secure, archive_public, notify_author_of_completion}. Do not deduplicate.","ground_truth":"draft_document, submit_for_review, revise_document, submit_for_review, archive_secure, notify_author_of_completion","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\A\\s*draft_document\\s*,\\s*submit_for_review\\s*,\\s*revise_document\\s*,\\s*submit_for_review\\s*,\\s*archive_secure\\s*,\\s*notify_author_of_completion\\s*\\Z","flags":["i"]},"tags":["conditional_branch","loop"],"notes":"L3: loop with branching; prompt requires listing repeated steps explicitly"}
