{"probe_id":"plan.backward_complement.L3.005","canonical_id":"plan.backward_complement","category":"plan","level":"L3","axis_values":{"n_known_parts":"3_plus"},"prompt":"A 1000 L tank is full at 9:00 and is leaking. From 9:00 to 11:00 the leak rate is 30 L/h. From 11:00 to 15:00 the leak rate is 50 L/h. From 15:00 to 20:00 the leak continues at a constant rate; the tank is exactly empty at 20:00. What is the leak rate (L/h) between 15:00 and 20:00? Output only the integer.","ground_truth":"148","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":148,"tolerance":0,"unit":"L/h","require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["complement","rate_time"],"notes":"2*30=60 + 4*50=200 = 260; remaining 740 L over 5 h = 148 L/h"}
